  canonical={pageUrl}
  ogType="article"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb
        items={[
          { label: 'Middle East', href: '/middleeast/' },
          { label: 'Oman Ports' },
        ]}
      />
      <span class="badge badge--amber">September 2026 updated</span>
      <h1>Oman Ports: Sohar &amp; Salalah intelligence for China freight</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A port-intelligence page for shippers routing China freight into Oman. This page explains the
        Sohar-vs-Salalah decision, the two UN/LOCODEs, the port roles and hinterland logic, how long
        China ocean moves take, what the destination cost stack looks like, and the 5% duty + 5% VAT
        clearance rules that apply at the Oman gate.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tldr">
        <p><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Oman runs two verified seaports — Sohar (OMSOH) for northern/Muscat cargo and Salalah (OMSLL) for southern/transshipment — both under a ×1.1025 stack (5% duty + 5% VAT), so the port split is a geography/resilience call, not a tax call. The statutory line equals the UAE’s ×1.1025 — $1,025 on $10,000 CIF — while the China→Sohar transit is a typical 19 days (15–30 range), 2 days faster than the UAE’s 21-day Jebel Ali benchmark. Because the snapshot publishes no Salalah-specific transit, the default rule is Sohar for Muscat/northern demand and Salalah only when Dhofar or transshipment is the actual destination.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="small muted">
        Confidence badges separate verified port codes and the GCC duty/VAT baseline from indicative
        routing and fee notes. Treat every LOW-confidence port, transit and fee note as a planning
        guide, and verify with the Oman port authority or your carrier before relying on it.
      </p>

      <div class="fact-grid mt-3">
        <div class="fact">
          <span class="fact-label">Ports</span>
          <span class="fact-value">Sohar / Salalah <ConfidenceBadge level="HIGH" /></span>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <span class="fact-label">UN/LOCODE</span>
          <span class="fact-value">{soharUnlocode} / {salalahUnlocode} <ConfidenceBadge level="HIGH" /></span>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
